# Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy / Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy are what make the
# page cross-origin isolated, which is what SharedArrayBuffer needs. DuckDB-wasm
# (AI Query + speed maps) runs threaded against it, and the transferable
# ReadableStream used to stream large PBF files into the worker needs it too.
#
# These only apply to responses served by the static-asset layer. Anything the
# Worker answers itself (/api/*, /samples/*) sets its own headers in code.
#
# Vite's hashed output lives under /assets/* and can be cached forever; the
# shell and service worker must always revalidate.

/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: cross-origin

/index.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/sw.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/registerSW.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/manifest.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# NOTE: /duckdb/* and /samples/* are not static assets. They are served from R2
# by the Worker (see worker/index.ts), which sets their headers in code.

/favicon.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/apple-touch-icon.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
